n started for  almost a year so there was a lot of  publicity around this a lot of emotions  so  i don't think it was a surprise when the  jury came back after five or six hours  of deliberation and found him guilty on  all of those counts that couldn't have  been a shock to him  and terry under a minnesota sentencing  guidelines for someone who does not have  a criminal record like derek shovin the  guidelines call for about a 12 and a  half year sentence but here prosecutors  asking for much more  what's their basis for that well they're  saying  obviously the judge did find that there  were aggravating factors not the least  of which was the  fact that there were children present  during this  whole incident and i think the  prosecution is looking at all of those  aggravating factors  and saying to the judge look we think  that you should give him more  more time all right thank you so much  now to florida where a manhunt is  underway for a suspect accused  of shooting a daytona beach officer in  the head  police say the officer is in critical  condition the department released the  officer's body cam video  from 9 p.m on wednesday the officer was  investigating a suspicious vehicle when  the driver got  out and a scuffle ensued the daytona  police  chief says the driver shot the officer  then took off  officers searched a nearby apartment and  reported finding  bulletproof vests guns and ammunition  the suspect has been identified  as 29 year old although wallace a 100  000  reward is being offered for information  leading to his capture  and arrest when we come back the latest  in the robert durst  trial what forensic evidence reveals  about the gun used to shoot surgeon  berman  and what she confided to a close friend  about her good friend  bobby durst  [Music]  and welcome back continuing coverage of  the trial of millionaire real estate  developer robert durst  where detectives say they still don't  have the murder weapon  durst is accused of shooting his best  friend susan berman in december 2000.  in court defense attorney dick de guerin  brought out the 22-caliber gun durst has  admitted he used to shoot his texas  neighbor morris black  durst also admits to owning a nine  millimeter gun the same type of weapon  believed to have been used to shoot  susan berman but on cross-examination  a now retired detective confirmed that  durst gun was not the same gun  that killed susan berman  nine millimeter that he was arrested  with and the shell  and you got it compared by a ballistics  expert  right yes and the result  was that gun was not the gun that fired  that bullet  there's no evidence that that gun was  the gun that fired that bullet  he wrote it up as inconclusive in  pasadena  right and you've tested it since then  haven't you i had gary jones fly the gun  out here to los angeles where we had it  tested by our firearms  by your own people and it was negative  wasn't it correct yes  okay next up on the witness stand was  lorraine newman a familiar name a close  friend of susan berman  and newman was one of the original cast  members of saturday night live  she's best known for her character  connie conehead  however there's nothing funny when she  testified that susan berman  confided in her that she had provided an  alibi for durst  when durst's wife disappeared  susan told me that she had provided an  alibi for her  for him for bobby do you specifically to  the best your memory recall  susan telling you that she had made a  phone call for bob  yes if i would ask you  um how certain are you not regarding the  time  but how certain are you that susan said  to you  that she had provided bob with an alibi  what would your response be 100  so terry austin if there's no murder  weapon in this case how's the  prosecution  prosecution going to prove that durst  was the killer  you know it's really hard when you don't  have the smoking gun so to speak  and you only have circumstantial  evidence and that's exactly what w